From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mod_mbedtls: seed the RNG before loading a key, without PSA too

network_mbedtls_load_pemfile() ran mod_mbedtls_init_once_mbedtls() only when
MBEDTLS_USE_PSA_CRYPTO is defined. Without it, mbedtls_pk_parse_key() and
mbedtls_pk_check_pair() are handed a CTR_DRBG that hasn't been seeded yet:
RSA keys don't use it there, but an EC key does, and lighttpd crashes
(NULL read) as soon as ssl.pemfile names an ECDSA certificate. Seed it first
in both builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/mod_mbedtls.c
+++ b/src/mod_mbedtls.c
@@ -1230,10 +1230,8 @@
 network_mbedtls_load_pemfile (server *srv, const buffer *pemfile, const buffer *privkey)
 {
-  #if defined(MBEDTLS_USE_PSA_CRYPTO)
     if (!mod_mbedtls_init_once_mbedtls(srv))
         return NULL;
-  #endif
 
     mod_mbedtls_kp * const kp = mod_mbedtls_kp_init();
     int rc;
 
